{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# DC index lag makes a crashed create produce a DUPLICATE Jira issue\n\n## Context / Problem\n\nThis is the only known defect where rebar writes WRONG DATA into Jira. Every other DC gap found so far\ncauses rebar to read incomplete data or fail loudly; this one silently creates a SECOND Jira issue for\nthe same local ticket — the exact outcome the write-ahead binding protocol exists to prevent.\n\n**Jira DC's Lucene index is eventually consistent.** Nodes poll for index changes roughly once per\nsecond and replication can fall arbitrarily behind; Atlassian's KB and JRASERVER-70423 document a\nreal-world lag of 2,991 seconds (~50 minutes). A JQL search cannot see an issue that is not yet\nindexed. Sound on Cloud, unsound on DC.\n\n**There are TWO index-dependent sites, and an earlier draft of this ticket named only the first.**\nThat matters, because fixing only the named one leaves the duplicate fully intact:\n\n1. `binding_store.recover_pending`, keyless branch (`binding_store.py:521-531`) — searches for the\n   `rebar-id:{local_id}` label and, on a miss, UNBINDS (\"the create never reached Jira\").\n2. `dispatch_one.create_one`'s dedup (`dispatch_one.py:237-238`) —\n   `hits = client.search_issues(f'labels = \"rebar-id:{local_id}\"')`, and on a miss it CREATES.\n\nSite 2 writes the duplicate. Site 1 only removes the record that might have prevented reaching it.\n\n**The chain, verified in source:**\n\n    a. crash during create               -> keyless-pending entry (jira_key: None)\n    b. next pass: recover_pending searches, misses (unindexed), UNBINDS\n    c. outbound_differ.py:528-531 gates the create on get_jira_key(local_id) is None\n    d. create_one dedup-searches, misses (unindexed), CREATES A DUPLICATE\n\n**Why fixing site 1 alone is insufficient.** Suppose (b) leaves the entry PENDING instead of\nunbinding. `get_jira_key` returns `entry.get(\"jira_key\")` (`binding_store.py:258-262`), which is\n`None` for a keyless-pending entry — so (c) still emits a create and (d) still misses. The duplicate\nhappens anyway. The pending entry is invisible to the only gate that decides whether to create.\n`is_pending()` already exists (`binding_store.py:270`) and the differ does not consult it.\n\nThe authors already engineered this hazard away where a key was known: the KEYED-pending branch's\ndocstring records \"NO Jira search — deterministic, so a hard crash in the create->label window yields\nNO duplicate.\" The keyless branch falls back to search precisely because no key exists.\n\n## Approach\n\n**Suppress the CREATE while a keyless-pending binding is inside an index-lag grace window, and stop\nunbinding on a single negative search.** Both halves are required and they do different jobs: the\ncreate gate is what prevents the duplicate; leaving the binding pending is what gives the gate\nsomething to see.\n\n1. **Record the evidence on the pending entry.** `recover_pending`'s keyless branch, on a negative\n   search, increments a `search_miss_count` and leaves the entry PENDING rather than unbinding. The\n   entry already carries `created_at` (`bind_pending`, `binding_store.py:289-297`), so its age is\n   available without a schema change beyond the counter.\n2. **Unbind only on corroborated absence.** Unbind when BOTH `search_miss_count >= 3` AND the entry is\n   older than an index-lag grace period (default 3600s, chosen to exceed the ~2,991s lag documented in\n   JRASERVER-70423). Until then the entry stays pending and the next pass retries. This converts a\n   silent duplicate into a delayed-but-correct answer.\n3. **Gate the create on pendingness, not just on the absent key.** `_compute_outbound_create_mutation`\n   is reached when `get_jira_key(local_id) is None`; it must additionally skip (defer, not drop) when\n   a keyless-pending binding for that local_id is younger than the grace period. This is the change\n   that actually prevents the second issue.\n4. `recover_pending` returns the count of RESOLVED bindings; an entry left pending is NOT resolved and\n   must not be counted, or the caller reads \"recovered\" as \"settled\".\n\n**Applied to BOTH vendors, not branched on DC.** Cloud's index is eventually consistent too — it is\nmerely faster, so the window is narrower rather than absent. A vendor branch would mean the safe path\nis the one exercised least, and the correctness property (never conclude non-existence from one\nunindexed search) is not vendor-specific. The cost on Cloud is a create deferred by at most one pass\nin a rare crash-recovery path.\n\n**Rejected: leaving the binding pending forever on repeated misses.** It is safer against duplicates\nbut a genuinely-never-created ticket would then never sync at all — trading a rare duplicate for a\npermanent silent omission. The corroboration rule bounds the wait instead.\n\n**Rejected: a non-indexed confirmation for the keyless branch.** There is none — JQL is the only way to\nfind an issue by label, and the keyless state is by definition the one with no key to GET. That is why\nthe keyed branch is already correct and this one cannot use the same trick.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/binding_store.py` — the keyless-branch miss counter, the\n  corroborated-unbind rule, an accessor exposing \"keyless-pending and within the grace window\", and the\n  resolved-count correction.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/outbound_differ.py` — consult that accessor before emitting a\n  create.\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/` — held-out regression tests (new module).\n\n## Testing\n\nThe oracle is a client that models the actual failure: the issue EXISTS but the search does not see it.\n\n* **the whole path, which is the only test that proves the fix** — a lagging-index client where\n  `create_issue` succeeds but `search_issues` returns empty. Drive crash -> recover -> differ -> create\n  and assert EXACTLY ONE issue is created. A test asserting only \"recover_pending did not unbind\"\n  passes today's code path while the duplicate is still written, which is the trap this closes.\n* **the create is deferred, not dropped** — once the index catches up (search starts returning the\n  issue), the next pass BINDS to the existing issue and still creates nothing.\n* **corroborated unbind still works** — a genuinely-never-created ticket, after 3 misses AND past the\n  grace window, unbinds and is then re-created, so the fix does not strand work forever.\n* **the keyed branch is untouched** — its no-search determinism is asserted unchanged.\n* **`recover_pending`'s return value** counts an entry left pending as NOT resolved.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] under a lagging-index client (create succeeds, search returns empty), the full\n      crash -> recover -> differ -> create path creates EXACTLY ONE issue, asserted by a test that\n      FAILS against the current code\n- [ ] the create gate consults keyless-pendingness, not only `get_jira_key(...) is None` — verified by\n      reading `outbound_differ`; a fix confined to `recover_pending` does NOT satisfy this\n- [ ] a single negative search never unbinds: unbinding requires >= 3 consecutive misses AND an entry\n      older than the grace period, both asserted\n- [ ] once the index catches up, the pending binding CONFIRMS against the existing issue and no second\n      issue is created, asserted\n- [ ] a genuinely-absent issue still unbinds after corroboration and is re-created, so no ticket is\n      stranded permanently pending\n- [ ] the KEYED-pending branch still performs NO search, asserted, since it is already correct\n- [ ] `recover_pending` does not count a still-pending entry as resolved\n- [ ] the Cloud path is asserted unaffected in behaviour beyond the deferral, since this changes shared\n      code\n- [ ] the reason (DC Lucene eventual consistency) is documented at both call sites so the next reader\n      does not \"simplify\" the grace window away"}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785519223642023001,"uuid":"01ee6d05-d751-4a9e-be58-6e0dad4b79e1"}